    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our definitive anchor, boasting an elite score of 83.29. Facing Matthews, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 14% platoon advantage and the rarity of a \"slow delivery\" pitcher, which significantly inflates his stolen base probability\u2014our scarcest and most coveted category. **Drake Baldwin** (68.18) also grades out exceptionally well; batting second against the vulnerable Zac Thornton (4.62 xERA) provides an ideal environment for him to capitalize on his elite xwOBA metrics. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** earns a strong start (63.14) by leveraging a 19% SP skill advantage against Lowder, proving that the optimizer values his favorable matchup and leadoff position over higher-projected bats in tougher spots.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Andy Pages** (58.24) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (58.66). While **Andy Pages** is a high-upside play, he narrowly misses the starting cut due to the superior matchup efficiency of our outfield and utility slots. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Wade Meckler**; while their assumed batting orders are baked into their scores, any late-breaking changes to those positions could negatively impact their efficiency. We remain cautious with **Heliot Ramos** (46.67), whose matchup against Miller has been dampened by a negative platoon shift, keeping him on the fringe of our active roster. We continue to hold **Jordan Westburg** and **Josh Jung** on the IL, while **Jacob Wilson**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Curtis Mead**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Luis Lara** remain on the bench as we preserve our game caps for higher-leverage matchups.",
